 not guaranteed between implementations using such values\\", and a registry whose purpose is interoperability should not mint digests a conforming verifier may be unable to read. The alphabets are enforced rather than assumed: base58btc excludes 0, O, I and l, and an earlier permissive pattern let three published examples carry digests that were not valid base58 at all. base58btc is RECOMMENDED, for consistency with `did:key` and `did:webvh`.","type":"string","minLength":16,"pattern":"^(z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]+|u[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)\$","examples":["zQmbWqxBEKC3P8tqsKc98xmWNzrzDtRLMiMPL8wBuTGsMnR"]},"Introductions":{"title":"Introductions","description":"Who may ask the community to introduce them to this member. `anyone`: any active member who can find the entry. `groups`: only members who share a community group with them. `connections`: only members holding an attributed, in-force verified relationship with them. `off`: nobody. A refused introduction is never reported to its sender.","type":"string","enum":["anyone","groups","connections","off"]},"Discoverability":{"title":"Discoverability","description":"The member\'s three discoverability decisions, made separately.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["listing","search","external"],"properties":{"listing":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Listing"},"search":{"type":"string","enum":["byName","exactNickname","off"],"description":"What a member\'s search may match. `byName`: `displayName` or `nickname`. `exactNickname`: only an exact `nickname`. `off`: nothing. A DID is never a search key for a non-administrator, whatever this says."},"external":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the member publishes a public card — the fields whose visibility is `public`, signed by the member — through the community\'s trust registry. A second consent, separate from registry-publication consent (`publishConsent`), which it requires. A community that cannot yet publish external cards refuses `true` with `notAvailable`."}}},"Listing":{"title":"Listing","description":"Whether members can find the entry. `listed`: it appears when members browse. `findable`: it does not appear when browsing, but a search that matches it under `search` returns it. `hidden`: no member finds it by browsing or searching; administrators still see it, and members who share a group that shows its members see it in that group\'s member list.","type":"string","enum":["listed","findable","hidden"]},"FieldVisibility":{"title":"FieldVisibility","description":"The audience the member chose for each field. A field with no entry here takes its definition\'s `defaultVisibility`. The community MUST NOT widen a member\'s choice: widening a field\'s ceiling or default changes no visibility already recorded.","type":"object","maxProperties":64,"propertyNames":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/FieldKey"},"additionalProperties":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Audience"}},"Audience":{"title":"Audience","description":"Who may see a directory field, ordered from narrowest to widest. `admins`: holders of `vtc.directory.admin` (and, for derived fields, `vtc.members.manage`). `groups`: members who share at least one community group with the subject (narrowed to the groups the subject names in `groupAudience`, where it names any). `connections`: members holding an attributed, in-force verified relationship with the subject at the community. `members`: every active member. `public`: anyone, and what the member\'s signed public card carries outside the community.\\n\\n`groups` and `connections` are not a chain: a viewer sees a field when they satisfy the audience the subject chose for it or any wider audience. Every audience includes the administrators, and the subject always sees their own whole card. There is no `onlyMe`: a value nobody else should see is not directory data.","type":"string","enum":["admins","groups","connections","members","public"]},"CardValues":{"title":"CardValues","description":"A card\'s stored values, keyed by field. Holds `member`-, `admin`- and `credential`-sourced fields only; derived fields (`role`, `joinedAt`, `did`, `personhood`) are read from the community\'s own records when a projection is made, never stored here. At most 64 values, and at most 16 KiB serialized excluding the blobs a `CardBlobRef` names.","type":"object","maxProperties":64,"propertyNames":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/FieldKey"},"additionalProperties":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/FieldValue"}},"FieldValue":{"title":"FieldValue","description":"The value of one field. Which shape a field takes is fixed by its definition\'s `type`: text-like types (`text`, `longText`, `url`, `email`, `phone`, `enum`, `date` as YYYY-MM-DD, `country` as ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, `did`) are strings; `multiEnum` and the base field `links` are arrays of strings; `image` and the base field `avatar` are a `CardBlobRef`; `claim` is a `VerifiedValue`; the derived base field `personhood` is a boolean.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"array","maxItems":32,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":500}},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/CardBlobRef"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/VerifiedValue"}]},"VerifiedValue":{"title":"VerifiedValue","description":"The value of a `credential`-sourced field: a claim the member disclosed from a credential they presented, with the issuer that attests it. A verified value always names its issuer, and a self-asserted value is never shaped as one. The community keeps only the disclosed claim and these facts about it — never the presentation.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["value","issuer","verifiedAt"],"properties":{"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"number"}],"description":"The disclosed claim value."},"issuer":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","maxLength":2048,"description":"DID of the credential\'s issuer, shown as the field\'s verification badge."},"credentialType":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"The most specific `type` of the credential the claim came from."},"verifiedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the community verified the presentation."},"validUntil":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the credential expires, where it does. The community withdraws the value once it passes."}}},"CardBlobRef":{"title":"CardBlobRef","description":"A content-addressed image held in the community\'s blob store — an avatar or an `image` field. At most 256 KiB, images only, re-encoded by the community on upload (vtc/directory/images/upload: metadata stripped, dimensions capped) so its digest does not link the member across communities. A viewer reads the bytes with vtc/directory/images/get, which answers only where the same projection shows the value. `url` and `urlExpiresAt` MAY appear in a projection: a short-lived URL the community checks against the same projection, so a member-only image is never a public URL. A community that does not offer one leaves both out.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["sha256","mediaType"],"properties":{"sha256":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}\$","description":"Lowercase hex SHA-256 of the stored, re-encoded bytes."},"mediaType":{"type":"string","enum":["image/png","image/jpeg","image/webp","image/avif"],"description":"Media type of the stored bytes."},"size":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":262144,"description":"Size in bytes of the stored bytes."},"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"description":"Projection only: a URL the viewer can fetch the image from until `urlExpiresAt`."},"urlExpiresAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Projection only: when `url` stops working."}}},"EntryId":{"title":"EntryId","description":"Opaque identifier of one directory entry: `dir_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, scoped to one community, and stable for the life of the membership — it survives a rotation of the member\'s DID, which is why groups, notes and cards are keyed by it. It MUST NOT be derived from, and MUST NOT reveal, any DID of the member, and the same person\'s entries in two communities MUST NOT share one. Compared by exact string equality.","type":"string","pattern":"^dir_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"}}}';

